# Digilent Basys 3 (Xilinx XC7A35T-1CPG236C), two pins of it.
#
# PROVENANCE: the pin names are transcribed from
# `examples/soc/board/basys3.rcf`, which transcribes Digilent's published
# `Basys-3-Master.xdc`. W5 is the board's single 100 MHz oscillator and
# its only clock source; U16 is LED 0.
#
# On 2026-09-24 a bitstream built with these two pins was loaded into a
# Basys 3 and the part reported `DONE` high with no CRC error. Nobody has
# watched the LED yet, so what the clock does on silicon is not confirmed.
# LVCMOS33 is the only IO standard any of this has been tried with.
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 clk W5
set_io -io_standard LVCMOS33 led U16
create_clock -name sys -period 10.0 clk
clock_domain sys clk
